.TH "UNICODE\-TAG" "1" "January 2020" "secure-terminal" "secure-terminal Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBunicode\-tag\fR \- tag deceptive Unicode in text for safe machine reading
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBunicode\-tag\fR [\fIFILE\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
unicode\-tag reads text \-\- from \fIFILE\fR arguments, or from standard input when none are given \-\- and writes it back byte\-for\-byte, except that every Unicode code point which could DECEIVE a reader is replaced, in place, by a self\-describing \fB[U+XXXX NAME]\fR token: bidi controls that reorder text, zero\-width and invisible characters, C0/C1 and DEL controls (including carriage return and ESC), and cross\-script homoglyphs posing as ASCII (scoped to a mixed\-script token, so an honest foreign word is left untouched)\.
.P
Honest text \-\- ASCII, accented Latin, CJK, emoji, whole\-script foreign words \-\- passes unchanged\. Newline and tab pass verbatim and a trailing newline is neither added nor removed\. An undecodable byte is tagged, not dropped\.
.P
It is meant for feeding untrusted text to a program or model that must not be fooled by, or silently relay, an active control code point\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 on an unreadable file or a closed output pipe\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBunicode\-tag\-stdin\fR(1), \fBsecure\-terminal\-cli\fR(1)
